From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:07:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read the status of a polled device under its lock

CCECBusDevice::TransmitPoll() read m_deviceStatus of the device that it
polls without that device's lock, while the threads that poll or ask that
device set it under the lock (SetDeviceStatus()). It now asks
IsHandledByLibCEC(), which reads it under the lock. What is decided does
not change.

Tests (outside the tree): libCEC built on the host with ThreadSanitizer,
with an amplifier that is polled while another thread asks it for its name
(a data race on m_deviceStatus before, none after).
---
 src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp b/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
index 510539a..d082a03 100644
--- a/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
@@ -976,7 +976,7 @@ bool CCECBusDevice::TransmitPoll(const cec_logical_address dest, bool bUpdateDev
     destination = m_iLogicalAddress;
 
   CCECBusDevice *destDevice = m_processor->GetDevice(destination);
-  if (destDevice->m_deviceStatus == CEC_DEVICE_STATUS_HANDLED_BY_LIBCEC)
+  if (destDevice->IsHandledByLibCEC())
     return bReturn;
 
   MarkBusy();
